WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.610
Speaker 1: So we have a new CBS News poll
asking American voters about a number of different

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:09.420
things, which we will look at, but one top
line that just cannot be missed is that at

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:14.080
this point in time, almost six months out
from the November 20, 20 election.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:20.750
Seventy five percent of Trump voters still
believe Donald Trump's lie that he won the

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.770
election, not Joe Biden.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:29.279
Seventy five percent of Trump voters responded
that, no, I do not consider Joe Biden the

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:32.820
legitimate winner of the 2020 election.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.710
It's almost as bad with Republicans.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:39.149
The idea that there's a big difference between
Republicans and Trump voters, 70 percent of

00:00:39.149 --> 00:00:46.600
Republicans overall do not believe that Joe
Biden is the rightful winner of the 2020 election

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:51.550
if the numbers are anywhere close to this.

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:57.780
In reality, it is another humiliating embarrassment
for the country and for critical thinking

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:58.910
in the United States.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:01.280
Now, what do I mean by if the numbers are
close to this?

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:08.649
In reality, it's an it's a reasonable question
to ask whether they actually believe it or

00:01:08.649 --> 00:01:13.929
they are showing support for their tribe by
claiming to believe it, even if they don't

00:01:13.929 --> 00:01:20.109
to send a message to the pollsters, to the
media, to Democrats, to whomever.

00:01:20.109 --> 00:01:23.099
It's a very stupid message to send if that's
what they're doing.

00:01:23.099 --> 00:01:27.560
But the problem is that even if they don't
actually believe it, but they just say they

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:36.359
do on polls, polling data like this can be
used to justify or to feign support for all

00:01:36.359 --> 00:01:40.250
sorts of things, either by protesters or by
Republican officials.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:41.419
So it's a problem.

00:01:41.419 --> 00:01:45.599
Either way, it's certainly conceivable that
there are some people who say they don't believe

00:01:45.599 --> 00:01:47.489
Joe Biden won, but they kind of do.

00:01:47.489 --> 00:01:50.649
And they're just saying it for the purposes
of messing with pollsters.

00:01:50.649 --> 00:01:56.600
Another issue we've covered how more voters
than in a long time have abandoned the Republican

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:57.600
Party.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.349
The percentage of people identifying as Republican
has gone down as a result.

00:02:01.349 --> 00:02:07.749
Does it make it more likely that the Trump
ists that stay are the ones most likely to

00:02:07.749 --> 00:02:12.150
believe any lie that Donald Trump tells and
that this is less a shift in the Republican

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.580
Party believing this?

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:19.260
It's just the people that still identify are
more of the Trump wing, which is why there's

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:25.030
only five points of difference between Republicans
and Trump supporters in this particular case.

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:26.030
That may be.

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:30.030
On the other hand, thanks to Trump, there's
lots of previous nonvoters who join the Republican

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:31.030
Party.

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.930
So maybe we can't make such an assessment.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:35.220
Other interesting data points from the poll.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:40.560
Despite the controversy in Washington, D.C.
about infrastructure spending, it's very popular.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:46.980
87 percent of the country wants to spend money
on improving roads and bridges overall.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:50.849
Fifty eight percent of the country approves
of Joe Biden's infrastructure.

00:02:50.849 --> 00:02:51.989
Big picture.

00:02:51.989 --> 00:02:58.849
That plan includes money for roads and bridges,
but also building our green infrastructure,

00:02:58.849 --> 00:03:04.120
hardening and improving the electrical grid,
modernizing building electric car chargers,

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:08.841
speeding up transitions to renewable energy,
many other great things that's popular, even

00:03:08.841 --> 00:03:13.019
though it's not clear a single Republican
will vote for it in the House or Senate, it's

00:03:13.019 --> 00:03:14.019
popular.

00:03:14.019 --> 00:03:17.890
Overall, Joe Biden has very high approval
on vaccine distribution.

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:22.530
72 percent of the country approves of the
job Biden has done on vaccines.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:28.239
Even nearly half of Republicans say Biden
has done well on vaccines, on vaccine hesitancy.

00:03:28.239 --> 00:03:34.469
The numbers, they improved marginally since
last month in the same poll, not by much.

00:03:34.469 --> 00:03:40.590
The number of people who are saying no to
the vaccine is steady at 22, similar to last

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.280
month, similar to other polls.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:48.579
The number who are maybes went down from 22
to 18 and the number of yes, went up from

00:03:48.579 --> 00:03:50.299
55 to 60.

00:03:50.299 --> 00:03:54.709
Not a massive change just outside the margin
of error.

00:03:54.709 --> 00:04:02.200
Those numbers, once we can vaccinate kids,
would get us very close if not to herd immunity.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:08.530
But it would obviously be far better if we
could get the vaccine hesitancy down to 12

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:09.619
or 15 percent.

00:04:09.619 --> 00:04:15.359
We have a much better chance if vaccine hesitancy
goes down to that degree.

00:04:15.359 --> 00:04:16.870
So that's the situation.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:17.870
Much of it is disturbing.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:23.520
I mean, it's very disturbing, of course, that
75 percent of Trump voters now almost six

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:27.960
months out from the election still are saying
that Donald Trump won.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:30.900
Most of those people want Trump back and would
vote for him again.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:36.169
As recent polling has shown us, you also don't
get to numbers like these without big boosts

00:04:36.169 --> 00:04:37.310
from media.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:41.979
And so we have to go back to Fox News and
to Newsmax and to O.J. and and others for

00:04:41.979 --> 00:04:46.840
boosting these conspiracies from day one after
the election, continuing to boost them until

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.370
they received lawsuit threats.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:54.990
And even today, they're still hosting guests
who say this exact same stuff.

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:59.570
The network anchors will sort of stay silent
and play more.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:04.771
Boy with it, but that's a big factor in how
people even came to believe this stuff, it's

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:07.240
not clear how we fix it.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:12.169
Lots of the people who still think Trump won
are the same people who won't wear a mask

00:05:12.169 --> 00:05:17.389
indoors, and they're the same people who won't
get a vaccine because they believe it's some

00:05:17.389 --> 00:05:22.440
kind of democratic plot to destroy liberty,
even though they also believe Trump invented

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:27.370
the vaccine or they think the vaccine will
be used to control their minds or poison them.

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:32.889
That's a pretty deep you could call it a delusion
or a misunderstanding, a fact that's deep

00:05:32.889 --> 00:05:33.949
and significant.

00:05:33.949 --> 00:05:36.160
And I don't really know how you fix that.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:41.319
And so maybe in that context, it's not super
shocking that you still see that level of

00:05:41.319 --> 00:05:47.000
the Republican Party believing Trump didn't
really lose, Joe Biden didn't really win.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:53.000
And what some of you are not going to believe
is that they are sort of going at it again

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.830
with the voter fraud stuff.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:56.919
Yeah, yes, they're doing it.

